.TH BZ3MORE 1 "2026-10-20" "bzip3-rs" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bz3more, bz3less, bz3most \- page possibly compressed files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bz3more
.RI [ files... ]
.br
.B bz3less
.RI [ files... ]
.br
.B bz3most
.RI [ files... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bz3more
pages the plain form of each named file.
A file starting with the
.B BZ3v1
magic is decompressed with
.B "bzip3 \-dcfq"
; any other file is read directly.
With no files, standard input is probed for the magic and paged.
.PP
The program name selects the pager:
.B bz3less
uses
.BR less ,
.B bz3most
uses
.BR most ,
and
.B bz3more
uses
.BR more .
Each file is announced with a
.I "------> FILE <------"
header. Between files the pager prompts with
.IR "--More--(Next file: FILE)" ;
answers
.B e
or
.B q
quit, while
.B s
skips the next file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bzip3 (1),
.BR more (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR bz3grep (1),
.BR bz3diff (1)
